<h2>Animate one element</h2>

<p>
  Give any tag <c>anim=zoom</c>, <c>delay=0.2</c>, <c>dur=0.7</c> and it comes in that way.
  Together with <c><step></c> it is a build, like PowerPoint's entrance effects:
</p>

<step>
  <p anim=fade>Fades in on the first click, no movement.</p>
</step>

<step>
  <p anim=zoom dur=0.7>Zooms in from a smaller size.</p>
</step>

<step>
  <p anim=pop out=4>Pops with a little overshoot, then leaves again on the fourth click.</p>
</step>

<notes>
  anim: fade | rise (default) | zoom | left | right | down | blur | pop | none. delay and dur are seconds; at=N sets the click, out=N the click where it disappears. A step passes its attributes to everything inside.
</notes>
